    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for these. they're okay, i guess, but some of them feel a bit generic—especially question 2 and 3. they sound a little bit like they're just trying to hit the buzzwords rather than actually asking something a candidate can give a real, detailed answer to. \n\ncan you try again? i need them to be even more specific and grounded in real-world scenarios. also, i'm seeing the \"score\" on my end is a bit low because some of the key terms aren't quite integrated enough into the actual substance of the questions. \n\ntry to make them feel more natural and less like a checklist, but make sure those core themes (innovative, teamwork, synergy, growth-mindset, collaboration) are really present in the context of the scenarios you create. i really need to see the \"high quality\" part of this.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely, let's work on refining the questions with a stronger grounding in specific scenarios and a clearer connection to the themes:\n\n1. Recall a situation where you played a pivotal role in leading a cross-functional team to develop a groundbreaking product feature. Can you detail that experience, including how you inspired innovative thinking and sustained teamwork throughout the project?\n\n2. Describe an occasion when you noticed a palpable lack of innovation within your team. How did you foster a growth mindset in the group, and can you provide examples of specific collaborative strategies you used to reinvigorate engagement and creativity among your colleagues?\n\n3. Share a tangible example of collaborative synergy you’ve encouraged in a culturally or even organizationally challenging environment. What steps did you take to bring together different perspectives and expertise, and what impact did it have on the project's success?\n\n4. Discuss the instance when you, as a team member, identified an unforeseen obstacle during a critical phase of a project. How did you employ collaboration and innovative thinking to navigate this challenge and help the team keep the project on track?\n\n5. Delve into a time when you believed strongly in a team's potential for significant growth. What actionable steps did you take to cultivate an environment where innovation, collaboration, and a growth mindset thrived",
      "source": "target",
